  "worked_solution": "To graph the function $y=4f(x),$ we take the graph of $y=f(x)$ and stretch it by factor of $4$ parallel to the $y$-axis. This has the effect of multiplying the $y$-coordinates of all points on $y=f(x)$ by $4.$\n\nThe resulting graph is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14218586/assets/a4b0c34ba1ed9036d8f42693e1c087f10df75e7fe27b1ad23d8885467de1cfab.png)",
